Fixed. All four checks green: build, test (4425 + 89 passed), clippy -D warnings, fmt.

**Root cause of the clippy error:** the implementation added the grade_forecast helper (empty forecast → None, never `Some(0.0)`) but never wired it into any call site — so it was dead code, and the inline empty-checks it was meant to replace were still duplicated at three grading paths.

What I changed (fixed the error by completing the wiring, not by suppressing it):

1. `src/commands_risk_snapshots.rs`
   • record_green_validation_to: replaced the inline if emerging.is_empty() { None } else { ...accuracy_of... } with `grade_forecast(&changed_refs, emerging).map(|(_, pct)| pct)`
   • `auto_validate_after_failure: same replacement via a match, preserving the (emerging_hits, Option<pct>)` shape used by the stderr comparison line
   • Added `test_grade_forecast_empty_list_is_ungraded_not_zero — pins that an empty forecast grades as None` (quiet-because-silent), while a populated-but-wrong forecast grades as a real Some(0.0) (distinct outcomes, the task's core experiment)

2. `src/commands_risk.rs`
   • CLI validate path (handle_risk_validate): replaced its inline empty-check with grade_forecast, keeping the reactive-vs-emerging stderr line only when the forecast was populated
   • Re-export list: added grade_forecast, dropped accuracy_of (no longer used outside commands_risk_snapshots.rs, where it remains the shared grading core called by grade_forecast)

Behavior is unchanged for legacy data — all three sites already returned None on empty lists; they now do it through one tested helper instead of three hand-rolled copies, so the "empty = ungraded" invariant can't drift per-site.
